Feature: Detect SQL injection on the timesheet user-search endpoint

  Background:
    Given "curl" is installed
    And the following profile:
      | name | value                                                  |
      | url  | http://__TARGET__/timesheet-devops/user/search-by-name |

  Scenario: A normal name is accepted (the endpoint is alive)
    When I launch a "curl" attack with:
      """
      curl -s -o /dev/null -w "%{http_code}" "<url>?name=John"
      """
    Then the output should contain "200"

  Scenario: A single quote breaks the SQL query (injection is possible)
    When I launch a "curl" attack with:
      """
      curl -s -o /dev/null -w "%{http_code}" "<url>?name=x%27"
      """
    Then the output should contain "500"
